From: NanoKVM OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: pull up SG2002 SDIO command and data pads

The NanoKVM PCIe AIC8800D80 does not answer CMD5 when CMD/DAT0-DAT3
retain the reset pull-down configuration.  Keep SD1_CLK unchanged and ask
the pin controller to select pull-up, while preserving the configured drive
strength and all other pad bits.

Set the board limit to 50 MHz.  The matching AIC driver policy caps its
vendor clock request to this host limit, so D80's 150 MHz feature constant
cannot bypass the board description.

The CV18xx pad has independent pull-up and pull-down bits.  Make the generic
bias operations mutually exclusive so bias-pull-up produces the observed
working 0x44 value from the 0x48 reset value instead of enabling both pulls.

---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-nanokvm-enhanced.dts | 11 ++++++++---
 drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c                |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-nanokvm-enhanced.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-nanokvm-enhanced.dts
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-nanokvm-enhanced.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-nanokvm-enhanced.dts
@@ -251,9 +251,14 @@
 };
 &pinctrl {
 	sdhci1_cfg: sdhci1-cfg {
-		sdio-pins {
+		sdio-clock-pins {
 			power-source = <3300>;
-			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_CLK, 0)>, <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_CMD, 0)>,
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_CLK, 0)>;
+		};
+		sdio-command-data-pins {
+			power-source = <3300>;
+			bias-pull-up;
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_CMD, 0)>,
 				 <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_D0, 0)>, <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_D1, 0)>,
 				 <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_D2, 0)>, <PINMUX(PIN_SD1_D3, 0)>;
		};
@@ -270,7 +275,7 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdhci1_cfg>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	bus-width = <4>;
-	max-frequency = <25000000>;
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	non-removable;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sd;
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
@@ -344,11 +344,19 @@ static int cv1800_pinconf_compute_config(struct sophgo_pinctrl *pctrl,
 		case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_PULL_DOWN:
 			FIELD_MODIFY(PIN_IO_PULLDOWN, &v, arg);
 			m |= PIN_IO_PULLDOWN;
+			if (arg) {
+				v &= ~PIN_IO_PULLUP;
+				m |= PIN_IO_PULLUP;
+			}
 			break;
 		case PIN_CONFIG_BIAS_PULL_UP:
 			FIELD_MODIFY(PIN_IO_PULLUP, &v, arg);
 			m |= PIN_IO_PULLUP;
+			if (arg) {
+				v &= ~PIN_IO_PULLDOWN;
+				m |= PIN_IO_PULLDOWN;
+			}
 			break;
 		case PIN_CONFIG_DRIVE_STRENGTH_UA:
 			ret = sophgo_pinctrl_oc2reg(pctrl, sp,
 						    priv->power_cfg, arg);
-- 
2.43.0
